WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.990
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book three.

2
00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:08.944
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.244 --> 00:00:14.369
Unit thirteen: World Travel. Today you will talk about travel dreams with would.

4
00:00:14.669 --> 00:00:17.240
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.711
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:23.667
Culture shock.

7
00:00:24.683 --> 00:00:27.983
Culture shock means feeling confused in a new culture.

8
00:00:28.583 --> 00:00:31.047
I had culture shock in Japan at first.

9
00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:34.639
Your turn. Say: Culture shock.

10
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:38.548
Culture shock.

11
00:00:39.283 --> 00:00:40.470
Global citizen.

12
00:00:41.483 --> 00:00:44.644
Global citizen means a person who cares about the whole world.

13
00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:47.424
Travel makes you a global citizen.

14
00:00:48.017 --> 00:00:51.191
Your turn. Say: Global citizen.

15
00:00:54.033 --> 00:00:55.441
Global citizen.

16
00:00:56.183 --> 00:00:57.126
Time zone.

17
00:00:58.117 --> 00:01:01.033
Time zone means an area with the same clock time.

18
00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:03.650
London is in a different time zone.

19
00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:06.960
Your turn. Say: Time zone.

20
00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:11.022
Time zone.

21
00:01:11.783 --> 00:01:12.935
Local custom.

22
00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:17.459
Local custom means a usual way of doing things in a place.

23
00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:20.073
Taking off shoes is a local custom.

24
00:01:20.683 --> 00:01:23.672
Your turn. Say: Local custom.

25
00:01:26.533 --> 00:01:27.801
Local custom.

26
00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:29.632
Cross-cultural.

27
00:01:30.617 --> 00:01:33.220
Cross-cultural means between different cultures.

28
00:01:33.817 --> 00:01:36.060
Cross-cultural friendships are special.

29
00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:39.627
Your turn. Say: Cross-cultural.

30
00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:43.746
Cross-cultural.

31
00:01:44.483 --> 00:01:45.461
Landmark.

32
00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:49.088
Landmark means a famous building or place.

33
00:01:49.683 --> 00:01:51.880
The Eiffel Tower is a famous landmark.

34
00:01:52.483 --> 00:01:54.822
Your turn. Say: Landmark.

35
00:01:57.667 --> 00:01:58.656
Landmark.

36
00:01:59.417 --> 00:02:00.987
Cuisine exploration.

37
00:02:01.983 --> 00:02:05.248
Cuisine exploration means trying many new kinds of food.

38
00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:08.569
Cuisine exploration is my favourite part of travel.

39
00:02:09.183 --> 00:02:12.695
Your turn. Say: Cuisine exploration.

40
00:02:15.533 --> 00:02:17.266
Cuisine exploration.

41
00:02:18.017 --> 00:02:19.285
Language barrier.

42
00:02:20.283 --> 00:02:24.349
Language barrier means a problem when people speak different languages.

43
00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:27.460
We used gestures to break the language barrier.

44
00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:31.097
Your turn. Say: Language barrier.

45
00:02:33.933 --> 00:02:35.527
Language barrier.

46
00:02:36.283 --> 00:02:37.296
Immersion.

47
00:02:38.283 --> 00:02:41.664
Immersion means living fully in a new language or culture.

48
00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:44.459
Immersion is the fastest way to learn.

49
00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:47.830
Your turn. Say: Immersion.

50
00:02:50.667 --> 00:02:51.598
Immersion.

51
00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:53.467
Backpacking.

52
00:02:54.483 --> 00:02:57.748
Backpacking means cheap travel with only a backpack.

53
00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:00.466
He went backpacking around Laos.

54
00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:03.342
Your turn. Say: Backpacking.

55
00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.259
Backpacking.

56
00:03:08.017 --> 00:03:09.111
Wanderlust.

57
00:03:10.117 --> 00:03:12.685
Wanderlust means a strong wish to travel.

58
00:03:13.283 --> 00:03:15.503
My wanderlust grows every year.

59
00:03:16.117 --> 00:03:18.502
Your turn. Say: Wanderlust.

60
00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:22.310
Wanderlust.

61
00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:24.132
Perspective.

62
00:03:25.117 --> 00:03:27.615
Perspective means a way of seeing things.

63
00:03:28.217 --> 00:03:29.972
Travel changed my perspective.

64
00:03:30.583 --> 00:03:33.456
Your turn. Say: Perspective.

65
00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:37.429
Perspective.

66
00:03:38.233 --> 00:03:41.582
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:42.417 --> 00:03:44.532
Visal, where would you love to travel?

68
00:03:45.617 --> 00:03:48.975
I would love to travel to Europe, maybe Italy.

69
00:03:50.083 --> 00:03:51.456
What would you learn there?

70
00:03:52.550 --> 00:03:55.409
I would learn new customs and try the cuisine.

71
00:03:56.517 --> 00:03:58.621
Would you worry about culture shock?

72
00:03:59.717 --> 00:04:03.109
A little, but immersion would give me a new perspective.

73
00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:05.871
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:06.717 --> 00:04:10.527
Grammar focus: would plus verb for hypothetical wishes.

75
00:04:10.827 --> 00:04:12.072
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:12.783 --> 00:04:14.667
I would love to travel abroad.

77
00:04:15.583 --> 00:04:17.327
I would learn new customs.

78
00:04:18.217 --> 00:04:19.694
Where would you go first?

79
00:04:20.633 --> 00:04:25.399
Use 'would' to talk about wishes and imagined situations. Short form: I'd.

80
00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:29.987
Be careful! Don't say: I would loved to travel abroad.

81
00:04:31.933 --> 00:04:34.223
Say: I would love to travel abroad.

82
00:04:34.523 --> 00:04:36.662
After 'would', use the base verb.

83
00:04:37.467 --> 00:04:40.049
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:40.833 --> 00:04:42.043
Seeing the World.

85
00:04:42.343 --> 00:04:45.388
Many teenagers have wanderlust and dream of world travel.

86
00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:49.294
Travelling abroad can give you culture shock at first.

87
00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:53.577
Exploring local customs and cuisine broadens your perspective.

88
00:04:54.567 --> 00:04:58.528
A language barrier is hard, but immersion helps you learn fast.

89
00:04:59.533 --> 00:05:02.996
I would love to go backpacking and become a true global citizen.

90
00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:08.206
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:11.038
I blank love to travel abroad.

92
00:05:11.338 --> 00:05:13.981
A, would. B, will. C, am.

93
00:05:17.533 --> 00:05:19.010
The answer is A: would.

94
00:05:20.150 --> 00:05:22.219
A strong wish to travel is blank.

95
00:05:22.519 --> 00:05:26.533
A, wanderlust. B, culture shock. C, immersion.

96
00:05:30.067 --> 00:05:32.565
The answer is A: wanderlust.

97
00:05:33.717 --> 00:05:36.088
Feeling confused in a new culture is blank.

98
00:05:36.388 --> 00:05:40.482
A, culture shock. B, a time zone. C, a landmark.

99
00:05:44.033 --> 00:05:46.068
The answer is A: culture shock.

100
00:05:47.267 --> 00:05:50.291
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:53.753
What would you like to learn from traveling abroad?

102
00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:03.865
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:04.165 --> 00:06:13.098
I would like to learn how people live in Japan. I would try their food, visit temples and practise speaking with local people.

104
00:06:13.398 --> 00:06:15.061
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:15.950 --> 00:06:21.934
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and would plus verb for hypothetical wishes.

106
00:06:22.234 --> 00:06:27.917
Today's value is open-mindedness. Be open to new places, people and ideas.

107
00:06:28.217 --> 00:06:30.997
See you in Unit fourteen. Goodbye!

108
00:06:31.297 --> 00:06:34.274
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

